    "created_at": "2016-06-02T02:03:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-02T02:04:16Z",
    "body": "I apologise for not being specific enough here. Firefox and Edge allow Ctrl-T, etc. to be captured via preventDefault(), and when you do this, they suppress the normal behaviour. I've edited the first comment to clarify.\n\nChrome and Safari do not let you preventDefault() these combinations in fullscreen.\n",
